Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:

$$
\begin{aligned}
2 x+\left(4 y\right)\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\
\left(4 y\right)\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\left(2 x\right) \\
\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\frac{2 x}{4 y}
\end{aligned}
$$

Evaluate the tangent slope at the given point:

$$
m_{\mathrm{t}}=-\frac{6}{8}=- \frac{3}{4}
$$

The tangent line uses $m=- \frac{3}{4}$.

Use the given point and this slope:

$$
\begin{aligned}
y-\left(2\right)&=- \frac{3}{4}\left(x-\left(3\right)\right) \\
y&=- \frac{3}{4}\left(x-\left(3\right)\right)+\left(2\right)
\end{aligned}
$$

At the $x$-axis, $y=0$. Substitute and simplify:

$$
\begin{aligned}
0&=- \frac{3}{4}\left(x-\left(3\right)\right)+\left(2\right) \\
x-\left(3\right)&=-\frac{2}{- \frac{3}{4}} \\
x&=\frac{17}{3}
\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore $P=\left(\frac{17}{3},0\right)$.

